### 5.2 Verified sample output

`go run . -in snapshot.json -v` produces:

```
prefix                          chosen peer     deciding attr
------------------------------  --------------  ----------------
<ip-address>/16                    <ip-address>        origin_validity
<ip-address>/24                    <ip-address>        med
<ip-address>/24                 <ip-address>        origin_validity
<ip-address>/24                  <ip-address>        origin_validity

poisoned / missing announcements:
  <ip-address>/16   <ip-address>   declared=valid    cache=invalid
  <ip-address>/16   <ip-address>   declared=notfound cache=invalid
  <ip-address>/24 <ip-address>  declared=valid    cache=notfound
  <ip-address>/24 <ip-address>   missing           (cache=valid)

minimal corrections that change the global egress map:
  <ip-address>/16 via <ip-address>
  <ip-address>/16 via <ip-address>
  <ip-address>/24 via <ip-address>
  <ip-address>/24 via <ip-address>
```

Reading the result:

* `<ip-address>/24` — `<ip-address>` had no stamp → conservative `invalid`, so `<ip-address>` won; repairing `<ip-address>` to `valid` makes it win on lower MED. One individually-impactful repair.
* `<ip-address>/24` — `<ip-address>` declared `valid` but the delta says `notfound`. Ranking it at face value let it win; the repaired map gives the prefix to `<ip-address>`. One repair.
* `<ip-address>/16` — cache `invalid`, but `<ip-address>` (`valid`) and `<ip-address>` (`notfound`) both lie. No single repair reaches the corrected winner (`<ip-address>`, lowest MED); the minimum is the coordinated pair `{<ip-address>, <ip-address>}` — the §2.6 case.
* `<ip-address>/24` — fully consistent, no repair.

### 5.3 Complexity

* Best-path selection: `O(P · A)` per prefix — linear.
* Poison scan: `O(paths)`.
* Minimal correction: exponential only in the number of *conflicting* paths per prefix (typically ≤ 4); prefixes are independent, so the global result is exact with no combined blow-up.
